-- title:
--   Crossing model for the completed node ring at j=0,1728
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, and let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $a \in k$ satisfy: $a$ lies in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$; $a^{q^2} = a$; and $a = 0$ or $a = 1728$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and put $A_0 := A \cap K$ (`coeffSubring A K`), with reduction $\mathrm{red}_K$ the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A_0$. Assume: $x \in A_0$ reduces to $a$; $\varpi \in A_0$ is such that $\mathrm{red}_K(c) = 0$ iff $\varpi \mid c$; $q = \varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$ in $A_0$ with $e_K \ge 1$ and $\varepsilon$ a unit; and every $l \in k$ with $l^{q^2} = l$ and $a\,(16l)^2(16l-1)^2 = 256\,((16l)^2 - 16l + 1)^3$ lifts to $A_0$. Let $R_0 :=$ `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A₀ red_K a (a ^ q)`, the subring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are $r, s \in A_0[X_0, X_1]$ with $s$ nonvanishing at $(a, a^q)$ under $\mathrm{red}_K$ and $f \cdot s(j, j_q) = r(j, j_q)$, where $X_0, X_1$ are evaluated at the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at level $1 \cdot q$; $R_0$ is assumed Noetherian and local. Set $W := A_0[[X]]/(X - \varpi)$ and let $\pi \in W$ be the class of the constant series $\varpi$, and $e :=$ `jWidth a` (equal to $3$ if $a = 0$, $2$ if $a = 1728$). Then there are a ring homomorphism $\theta : W[[X_0, X_1]] \to \widehat{R_0}$ into the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $R_0$ and a ring isomorphism $\iota : \widehat{R_0} \cong W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi^{e\,e_K})$ (the model `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ (jWidth a * eK))`) such that: $\theta$ is surjective; for $o \in A_0$, $\theta$ of the constant series of the class of $o$ is the image in $\widehat{R_0}$ of the constant $o \in R_0$; for every $o \in W$, $\iota(\theta(\mathrm{C}\,o))$ is `UVCrossingModel.const` of $o$; and $\iota$ carries the ideal of $\widehat{R_0}$ generated by the images of $\varpi$ and of $j_q - j^q$ onto the ideal generated by `UVCrossingModel.const` of $\pi$ together with `UVCrossingModel.U`, and the ideal generated by the images of $\varpi$ and of $j - j_q^q$ onto the ideal generated by `UVCrossingModel.const` of $\pi$ together with `UVCrossingModel.V`.
--
--   This is the local model of the plane modular curve $X_0(q)$ at a supersingular point with extra automorphisms, in the form of Deligne–Rapoport and Mazur–Rapoport: after completion the descended node ring becomes $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^{e\,e_K})$ with $e = 3$ at $j = 0$ and $e = 2$ at $j = 1728$, with the two level-one branch ideals $(\varpi, j_q - j^q)$ and $(\varpi, j - j_q^q)$ going to the two coordinate branches. It is the completion-side input for [`ModularCurve.exists_crossingPresentation_modularLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_crossingPresentation_modularLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728), from which the crossing presentation at wide nodes is obtained.
